                    ]]></description>    <styleUrl>#31_r</styleUrl>   <Point>     <coordinates>8.7803,46.7311,0</coordinates>   </Point>  </Placemark></Folder><Folder><name><![CDATA[Ancient Temple]]></name><open>0</open>
<Placemark>   <name>Roman temple district Petinesca</name>   <description><![CDATA[
        <b>Type:</b> Ancient Temple <b>County/Region:</b> Bern <b>Alt Name:</b> Römischer Tempelbezirk Petinesca <br /> Pos Accuracy: <b>5</b> Condition: <b>2</b> (5 is best)   Ambience: <b>4</b>  Access: <b>4</b>  (5 is best)<br />
                    <b>Lat:</b> 47.111833 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Long</b>: 7.2915<img src="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/a558/a312/gallery/Roman/Switzerland/thumb/hcj_IMG_6400.JPG" align="right" valign="top"></a>
<br />
                    Ancient Temple in Bern. Auf dem geschichtsträchtigen Jäissberg ist diese sehenswerte Römische Tempelanlage zu sehen. Es ist anzunehmen dass sie auf einer frühgeschichtlichen, keltischen Anlage hin...<b>.</b> (c) Meg. Portal contributors.<br />
		     <a href="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/article.php?sid=37594" >Link To More Information</a><br />
                    ]]></description>    <styleUrl>#64_r</styleUrl>   <Point>     <coordinates>7.2915,47.111833,0</coordinates>   </Point>  </Placemark></Folder><Folder><name><![CDATA[Ancient Village or Settlement]]></name><open>0</open>
<Placemark>   <name>Attinghausen-Geissrüggen Siedlungsplatz</name>   <description><![CDATA[
        <b>Type:</b> Ancient Village or Settlement <b>County/Region:</b> Uri <br /> Pos Accuracy: <b>3</b> Condition: <b>2</b> (5 is best)   Ambience: <b>5</b>  Access: <b>2</b>  (5 is best)<br />
                    <b>Lat:</b> 46.8438 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Long</b>: 8.5709<img src="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/a558/a312/gallery/Central_Europe/Switzerland/thumb/Attinghausen-Geissrüggen_4867.jpg" align="right" valign="top"></a>
<br />
                    Ancient Settlement in Uri Canton, Switzerland. Attinghausen-Geissrüggen Siedlungsplatz is an ancient settlement site tentatively dated to between 5th to 7th century BC on the hiking trail from Atting...<b>.</b> (c) Meg. Portal contributors.<br />
		     <a href="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/article.php?sid=45589" >Link To More Information</a><br />
                    ]]></description>    <styleUrl>#2_r</styleUrl>   <Point>     <coordinates>8.5709,46.8438,0</coordinates>   </Point>  </Placemark>
<Placemark>   <name>Augusta Raurica</name>   <description><![CDATA[
        <b>Type:</b> Ancient Village or Settlement <b>County/Region:</b> Baselland <b>Alt Name:</b> Augusta Raurica, Römische Siedlung <br /> Pos Accuracy: <b>5</b> Condition: <b>2</b> (5 is best)   Ambience: <b>4</b>  Access: <b>5</b>  (5 is best)<br />
                    <b>Lat:</b> 47.533161034949 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Long</b>: 7.7221709489822<img src="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/a558/a312/gallery/Roman/Switzerland/thumb/dgt_IMG_8764.JPG" align="right" valign="top"></a>
<br />
                    Ancient Settlement in Baselland. A 2000-year-old settlement on the southern bank of the Rhine, close to Basel. Named after the Celtic Rauriker tribe and the Roman Emperor Augustus. In its heyday the c...<b>.</b> (c) Meg. Portal contributors.<br />
